From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:16:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot: floating-point and vector memory instructions,
 byte/halfword exclusives (blockers 3 and 4)

The runtime defines __remill_fpu_exception_* (floating-point arithmetic was lifted but could not link, so
it ran in the JIT); the vector registers, FPCR and FPSR go in and out of Aot.run. test_aot_simd assembles
each instruction with aarch64-linux-gnu-as, lifts it alone and compares it with Unicorn on edge-value
vector registers: 48 memory forms, 175 scalar FP, 54 exclusives and barriers. module_validate gets a census
(every distinct instruction of a module, lifted or not) and random vector registers in its differential
run. On Balatro: 0.91% -> 0.55% of instructions unlifted, 88.6% -> 97.4% of functions liftable, main's
entries left to the JIT 14.1% -> 3.5%. The Remill patch is fork en cours/remill-patches/0004.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: floating-point and exclusive-access coverage of the AArch64 -> x86_64 recompilation (NX2Linux); no game data in the tests
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch feat/teo-t7-module-reel)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
